  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">223938_ALERT 904 Sierra Leone (Anticipation of Mpox outbreak)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposed Mpox anticipation project is designed to prepare communities in light the urgent health needs of Sierra Leones affected populations focussing on the current hotspot districts of Western Area Urban, Rural and Tonkolili through targeted enhanced coordination, surveillance, RCCE, and IPC. The project draws on lessons learned from previous outbreaks and incorporates the needs and perspectives of the affected population, ensuring that interventions are culturally sensitive, responsive, and effective. By prioritizing vulnerable groups and utilizing a community-driven approach, the project aims to mitigate the spread of Mpox and protect the most at-risk populations from severe outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
